The provided page covers only installation and a basic constructor example. It doesn't document React props, the full config shape, themes, CSS variables, realtime methods (`setSeries`, `update`, `dispose`), performance tips, or required CSS imports, so I can't give those without guessing.

**Install:**

```
npm i @gravity-ui/yagr
```

**Basic NPM usage (verbatim from the page):**

```typescript
import Yagr from '@gravity-ui/yagr';

new Yagr(document.body, {
    timeline: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5],
    series: [
        {
            data: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5],
            color: 'red',
        },
        {
            data: [2, 3, 1, 4, 5],
            color: 'green',
        },
    ],
});
```

**Script tag usage** is also shown on the page, using `https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/yagr/dist/yagr.iife.min.js`.

**Where to find the missing details:**

- Versioned docs for this release: `https://gravity-ui.com/llms/yagr/5.3.1/llms.txt`. The page says to use the URL matching the version in your `package.json`. For any 5.x install, the latest 5.x docs are at `https://gravity-ui.com/llms/yagr/5/llms.txt`.
